  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In the first step, alcohol group accepts a proton from the hydronium ion, and thus leaves forming a carbocation. As there is a chance for formation of a six-membered ring, a six membered ring is formed with a carbocation. Hydrogen next to the carbocation leaves forming a cycloalkene which is also the saytzeff product. Chain of reactions are as follows:</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5dc76dec-a96f-4270-a7d9-69af5342196e-969e45db-c6d5-4ace-bc99-d5c20859a8ea-9884748_2.png\" style=\"width: 812px; height: 272px;\" />&nbsp;</p>",
